Thanks. v9 uses it. remotes.env now percent-encodes the login and
password with jq's @uri, the awk userinfo script is gone, and
instance.conf lists textproc/jq among the packages. The series is
"[PATCH v9 0/6] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the mail relay jail"
[1].

I tested the encoding here with jq 1.8.2 in lab-claude. A creds line
of "me@p7x.dev p@ss:w/rd #x y%" gives the userinfo
me%40p7x.dev:p%40ss%3Aw%2Frd%20%23x%20y%25. I have not looked inside
lab-mail, so that its jq behaves the same is inference.

One thing is weaker than the awk script. A creds line with no space
used to fail at start with a message; with cut it gives the whole
line as both login and password, and Fastmail rejects the login at
the first send. The cover letter notes it. If you want the earlier
check back, a one-line test in remotes.env would do it.

